# Web-to-Android App Conversion

**Intent:** Ship a **web-first** product to Google Play with correct graphics, themes, and a thin native shell — without duplicating game logic in Kotlin. Reference implementations: **Equalize** (`equalize-android` WebView shell) and **DSA Patterns** (`dsapatterns-website` Capacitor wrapper).

**Cross-refs:** Game embed/PWA rules → `games-building.mdc`. Host site vendoring → `website-building.mdc`. UI/a11y baseline → `universal-product.mdc` §2a.

---

## §1 Architecture — web owns the product **[core]**

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Game logic, UI, levels, themes, copy | Web (`*.html`, React/Vite `dist/`, inline JS) |
| Splash, launcher icons, signing, Play packaging | Android shell |
| Back navigation | Web stack (`GameBack` / `EqualizeBack` + History API) + Android `OnBackPressedCallback` |
| Timer pause on background | Web (`visibilitychange`) + Android `onPause`/`onResume` |
| Release hardening (strip debug globals) | Gradle pipeline |
| Offline first launch | Bundled `file:///android_asset/…` or Capacitor `webDir` |

**Do not** duplicate gameplay, levels, colors, or dashboard behavior in native Kotlin.

### Three shells we use

| Pattern | When | Sync |
|---------|------|------|
| **Thin WebView shell** | Single HTML game (Equalize) | Gradle `sync*WebAssets` copies curated files into `app/build/generated/…` on every asset merge |
| **TanStack SPA WebView** | Vite/Nitro CSR game (Circuit Flow, Train Panic, …) | `build-android-standalone.mjs` → `dist/android-client/` → Gradle sync (see §14) |
| **Capacitor** | Full React/Vite portal SPA (DSA Patterns) | `npm run build` → `npx cap copy android` (or `cap sync android` after plugin/native config changes) |

Pick one per product. Do not mix Capacitor plugins into a hand-rolled WebView shell without an ADR.

### WebView shell constraints

- **Equalize (static HTML):** load bundled entry via `WebViewAssetLoader` or `file:///android_asset/<entry>.html` — **no network** on first launch in release.
- **TanStack SPA:** load `https://appassets.androidplatform.net/assets/` (trailing slash) via `WebViewAssetLoader` + custom `SpaAssetsPathHandler` (§14). Do **not** use `…/assets/index.html` as `game_url` without SPA fallback — empty path must map to `index.html`.
- **Skip service worker** on `file://` / offline bundles (register only on HTTP/HTTPS hosts).
- **No `INTERNET` permission** if fonts and assets are self-hosted in the bundle.
- `allowBackup="false"` when local scores/progress must not cloud-restore (anti-tamper).
- Release builds **strip** debug globals (`window.*Debug`, `?e2e=1` shortcuts) via Gradle — never ship auto-win hooks in release AABs.
- Use `WebViewAssetLoader` for same-origin asset paths; block external navigation in `shouldOverrideUrlLoading`.
- Disable zoom controls; enable `domStorageEnabled` for `localStorage`.
- Generic back bridge: expose `window.GameBack.handle()` (returns `true` if web consumed back); Kotlin calls it before `finish()`.

