## §11 Mobile UX & Input Conversion **[core]**

When porting a web game to Android, Cursor MUST automatically audit and refactor the UX for mobile constraints:

- **Input Refactoring:** Strip all Keyboard (`WASD`/Arrow keys) and `hover`-state event listeners. Replace them with single-tap, swipe-to-move, or virtual floating joystick logic using touch events (`touchstart`, `touchmove`).
- **Kill On-Screen D-Pads:** Do NOT implement visible on-screen directional buttons unless explicitly requested. Prioritize frictionless gesture-based mechanics.
- **Mobile Safe Areas:** Ensure all Canvas and DOM elements respect Android safe areas. Critical UI (scores, back buttons) MUST NOT render in the top 40px (notches/status bar) or bottom 40px (gesture bar).
- **Instant Restart Loop:** Remove multi-step 'Game Over' modals. On failure, implement a maximum **0.5-second reset loop** to allow instant, frictionless replayability.

