## §2 Five in-game themes (Equalize standard) **[core]**

**Scope:** Equalize and games that ship an **in-app theme switcher**. If there is no switcher, do **not** claim theme count on Play (§13).

We ship **five** player-selectable themes. Persist choice in `localStorage` (e.g. `eq_theme`). Update `<meta name="theme-color">` on switch for Android status-bar harmony.

| ID | Label | `data-theme` | Background / mood | Notes |
|----|-------|--------------|-------------------|-------|
| **balance** | ⚖️ Balance | `balance` | `#0A0A0A` black, purple/crimson/gold | **Default for Play Store** — dark, premium |
| **ember** | 🔥 Ember | `ember` | `#1A0A0A` warm dark, orange accents | High contrast on dark |
| **zen** | ☀️ Zen Sand | `zen` | `#F5F0E8` cream paper | **Light theme** — audit all tutorial/game text (see §6) |
| **midnight** | 🌙 Midnight | *(remove `data-theme`)* | `#1A1A2E` indigo night | Uses `:root` jewel-spectrum tiles |
| **ocean** | 🌊 Ocean | `ocean` | `#0A1628` deep blue | Cool palette |

Cycle order in UI: `balance → ember → zen → midnight → ocean`.

**Screenshot / Play Store rule:** Capture store screenshots in **Balance** (or the theme shown in the icon) so listing matches first launch. If the icon is dark/gold, do not lead with Zen Sand screenshots unless the default theme is Zen.

