## §14 TanStack SPA → standalone WebView (Bharat Brawlers) **[core]**

When porting TanStack Start / Vite / Nitro games into per-game Play shells (`games/<Name>/android/`), follow this pipeline. **Embed builds are not Play builds.**

### Framework CLI (14 games, excludes Equalize)

Registry: `Bharat Brawlers/scripts/games/android/registry.mjs`. Skill: `.agents/skills/webapp-to-android/SKILL.md`.

```bash
# One command — default: patch, web build, Gradle, icons
node scripts/games/android/run.mjs <slug|--all> [--scaffold] [--screenshots] [--smoke]

npm run android:all          # from Bharat Brawlers root
node scripts/games/android/audit-parity.mjs
```

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `run.mjs` | Orchestrator |
| `patch-web.mjs` | `ANDROID_STANDALONE` vite/router/`__root` |
| `apply-theme-parity.mjs` | 5-theme `ThemeSwitcher` (§13 discoverability) |
| `build-web.mjs` | `dist/android-client/` (`.output/public` or `dist/client`) |
| `capture-screenshots.mjs` | 1080×2400 via `screenshot-scenes.mjs` |

Legacy shims: `build-android-standalone.mjs` → `run.mjs`.

### Canonical output chain

```
games/<Name>/src  →  build-android-standalone.mjs  →  dist/android-client/  →  Gradle sync  →  AAB
```

| Output | Purpose | Play? |
|--------|---------|-------|
| `dist/client` + embed `index.html` | dsapatterns.io iframe (`DSAPATTERNS_EMBED=1`, `*-embed` HTML class) | **No** |
| `dist/android-client` | Offline WebView bundle (`ANDROID_STANDALONE=1`, no embed class) | **Yes** |

### Web build env (`build-android-standalone.mjs`)

```bash
ANDROID_STANDALONE=1
VITE_ANDROID_STANDALONE=1
VITE_ANDROID_BASE=/assets/
# Unset: DSAPATTERNS_EMBED, VITE_EMBED_SLUG, GAME_SLUG
```

**`vite.config.ts`:** when `ANDROID_STANDALONE=1`, set `base: '/assets/'` and Nitro `baseURL: '/assets/'` (mirror embed branch).

**`router.tsx`:** `routerBasepath()` prefers `import.meta.env.VITE_ANDROID_BASE`, then embed slug, then `BASE_URL`.

**`__root.tsx`:** omit `*-embed` HTML class when `VITE_ANDROID_STANDALONE=1` so home/leaderboard routes stay reachable.

**`gameBack.ts`:** register `window.GameBack.handle()` — router back if possible, else return `false` for Kotlin `finish()`.

### Post-build patches (do not skip)

1. **`patch-android-client.mjs`** — TanStack CSR hydrate/bootstrap fixes; set router `basepath:"/assets/"`. **Critical:** `rewriteAssetUrls` also rewrites `basepath` to `./assets/` — restore literal `basepath:"/assets/"` after that pass or WebView lands on `/assets/assets` → 404.
2. **`generate-android-index.mjs`** — static CSR shell: `<base href="./"/>`, `start_url: "./"`, **no** `*-embed` class on `<html>`, strip `/index.html` from pathname via inline script.
3. **Offline verify** — grep bundle for CDN hosts (`fonts.googleapis.com`, etc.).

### Gradle asset sync (common failure)

In `app/build.gradle.kts`:

```kotlin
// projectDirectory = games/<Name>/android/app  →  use ../../dist/android-client
val webClientDir = layout.projectDirectory.dir("../../dist/android-client")
val syncedGameAssets = layout.buildDirectory.dir("generated/gameAssets")

val syncGameWebAssets by tasks.registering(Sync::class) {
    from(webClientDir)
    into(syncedGameAssets)
}

android {
    sourceSets {
        getByName("main") {
            assets.srcDir(syncedGameAssets)   // NOT debug/release sourceSets (AGP 8.13)
        }
    }
}

tasks.named("preBuild").configure { dependsOn(syncGameWebAssets) }
```

**`strings.xml`:** `game_url` = `https://appassets.androidplatform.net/assets/` (trailing slash, not `index.html`).

### `SpaAssetsPathHandler` (SPA fallback + empty path)

TanStack routes (`/play`, `/leaderboard`) and trailing-slash entry URLs need `index.html` fallback. **Use paths without a leading slash** for `AssetsPathHandler.handle`.

```kotlin
class SpaAssetsPathHandler(context: Context) : WebViewAssetLoader.PathHandler {
    private val assetsHandler = WebViewAssetLoader.AssetsPathHandler(context)

    override fun handle(path: String): WebResourceResponse? {
        val assetPath = when {
            path.isEmpty() || path == "/" -> "index.html"
            path.startsWith("/") -> path.removePrefix("/")
            else -> path
        }
        assetsHandler.handle(assetPath)?.let { return it }
        val leaf = assetPath.substringAfterLast('/')
        val hasExtension = leaf.contains('.') && !leaf.startsWith('.')
        if (!hasExtension) return assetsHandler.handle("index.html")
        return null
    }
}
```

Register: `.addPathHandler("/assets/", SpaAssetsPathHandler(this))`.

### Repo hygiene

Gitignore per shell: `**/android/.gradle/`, `**/android/local.properties`, `**/android/app/release-key.keystore`, `**/android/**/build/`.

**Launcher icons:** resize `playstore-icon.png` per mipmap density (`resize-launcher-icons.mjs` / `sips`) — do not copy one 500KB PNG into every `mipmap-*` folder.

**`gradle-wrapper.jar`:** must be a valid wrapper JAR (`no main manifest attribute` = corrupt copy). Copy from a known-good Android project if needed.

### Espresso / WebView tests

- Assert bundled `index.html` / `manifest.webmanifest` via `targetContext.assets.open(...)`.
- Poll `evaluateJavascript` until content appears (`pollUntilJs`, ~45s) — single-shot checks flake on cold WebView + React hydrate.
- Use `data-testid` + router navigation; avoid assumed globals (`renderLeaderboard`, etc.).

### E2E flags in minified release bundles

When `esbuild: { drop: ["console"] }` strips `if (isE2eMode()) { console.log(...) }` entirely, preserve checks via side effects:

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (typeof window !== "undefined") {
    (window as any).__e2e_active = isE2eMode();
  }
}, []);
```

Gate **release** Play builds: strip `?e2e=1` auto-win paths in Gradle `stripReleaseAssets`; do not list e2e-only flows on Play.

### Screenshot automation

`capture-android-screenshots.mjs` + `android-preview-server.mjs` serve `dist/android-client` at `/assets/` (1080×2400). Use `?e2e=1` and `addInitScript` for deep routes. **Final Play screenshots** must come from **release AAB** on emulator (§13), not preview server alone.

### Equalize-style mistakes to avoid (TanStack shells)

| Mistake | Prevention |
|---------|------------|
| Sync from wrong repo / Capacitor `android/` | Gradle `from` = `../../dist/android-client` only |
| Ship embed bundle to Play | Separate `android-client` pipeline; no `*-embed` class |
| Listing “modes” / themes / leaderboard | §13 matrix from code; omit if no switcher or hidden UI |
| `game_url` → `index.html` without empty-path handler | Trailing-slash URL + `SpaAssetsPathHandler` normalize |
| Fake / composited screenshots | Emulator from release APK/AAB only |
| `com.dsapatterns.*` on standalone game | Per-game `applicationId` (e.g. `com.circuitflow.puzzle`) |

### Phase 8 — Native shell & Play Vitals hardening **[applicable if Android native shell]**

Patterns from modern WebView wrappers (`shiaho777/web-to-app`, `Jipok/website-to-apk`, `Drjacky/claude-android-ninja`). Bharat Brawlers enforces via `apply-native-hardening.mjs` + `audit-native-hardening.mjs`.

| Concern | Requirement |
|---------|-------------|
| **Predictive back (API 33+)** | `onBackPressedDispatcher.addCallback` — never override deprecated `Activity.onBackPressed()` |
| **Play Vitals ANR** | No blocking disk I/O in `onCreate`; defer `webView.loadUrl` with `webView.post { }` to keep start-to-interactive under ~2s |
| **16 KB page size (API 35+)** | If adding NDK `.so` libs, link with `-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384` (CMake: `ANDROID_SUPPORT_FLEXIBLE_PAGE_SIZES=ON`) |
| **WebView immersion** | Double-back exit, `Intent.ACTION_VIEW` for external schemes, `mediaPlaybackRequiresUserGesture = false`, hardware acceleration, portrait lock, `shortEdges` cutout |
| **Intent redirection security** | Strip `component`/`selector` from parsed intents; sanitize with `androidx.core.content.IntentSanitizer` before `startActivity()` |
| **IME soft input** | `android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"` on `<activity>` so keyboards resize the canvas on Android 15+ edge-to-edge |
| **AGP 9 future-proofing** | `preBuild` → `Sync` into `layout.buildDirectory.dir("generated/gameAssets")` — not deprecated per-variant `assets` sourceSet hacks |

Canonical Kotlin/manifest snippets: `Bharat Brawlers/scripts/games/android/native-hardening-template.mjs`.

