## §15 Android Studio test & Play Store publish **[core]**

End-to-end checklist from **first open in Studio** through **Production** (or Internal testing). Run on **each** game shell before upload.

### A. One-time machine setup

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| JDK | **JDK 17** — `brew install openjdk@17` or use Android Studio’s embedded JDK (Settings → Build → Gradle → Gradle JDK). CLI: `export JAVA_HOME="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home"` |
| Android Studio | Latest stable; install **SDK Platform 35** + **Build-Tools** via SDK Manager |
| Emulator | Device Manager → create phone AVD (e.g. Pixel 7, API 34+) |
| Play Console | [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console) — developer account ($25 one-time) |

### B. Build web assets (every web change)

From **game monorepo root** (e.g. Bharat Brawlers):

```bash
node scripts/games/build-android-standalone.mjs <slug>
# slug: circuit-flow | train-panic | grid-tower-defense | pocket-park-tycoon | tank-wars
```

Output: `games/<Name>/dist/android-client/`. Gradle syncs this on next build (§14).

### C. Open project in Android Studio

1. **File → Open** → `games/<Name>/android/` (the folder containing `settings.gradle.kts`, not the repo root).
2. Let Gradle sync finish. If sync fails on JDK 25, set Gradle JDK to **17** in Settings.
3. Confirm `local.properties` exists with `sdk.dir=…` (gitignored; Studio creates it).
4. **Optional CLI sanity check** (faster than Studio for CI):
   ```bash
   cd games/<Name>/android
   ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
   ```

### D. Run on emulator or device (debug)

1. Start AVD or connect USB device (USB debugging on).
2. Select **app** configuration → **Run** (green play).
3. **Smoke test (offline):** enable airplane mode → force-stop app → cold launch → game home/play loads (no blank WebView).
4. Tap **back** — overlays/routes dismiss before app exits (`GameBack`).
5. Run instrumentation tests (Circuit Flow / Train Panic):
   ```bash
   ./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest
   ```
   Or full scripted pass: `node scripts/games/test-android-standalone.mjs` from repo root.

### E. Build signed release AAB

**Do not upload debug APKs to Play.** Use the **production keystore** (back up securely — loss = cannot update the app). Play Store requires **App Bundle (.aab)**, not APK.

#### Production keystore (shared across all Bharat Brawlers games)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Keystore file | `Untitled.jks` — stored at `/Users/deepanshrawal/Documents/git/Untitled.jks` (outside repo — never commit) |
| Key alias | **`equalize@1`** |
| Store/key password | _(ask maintainer — store in a password manager)_ |

#### Android Studio (recommended first time)

1. **Build → Generate Signed Bundle / APK…**
2. Select **Android App Bundle** → **Next**
3. Key store path: browse to `Untitled.jks`
4. Key alias: `equalize@1`  ·  Key store password & Key password: _(ask maintainer)_
5. Build variant: **release** → **Finish**
6. Output: `app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab`

#### CLI / CI (repeat uploads)

```bash
# From repo root — builds web + signed AAB in one command
KEYSTORE_PATH="/Users/deepanshrawal/Documents/git/Untitled.jks" \
KEYSTORE_PASSWORD="your-secure-password" \
KEY_ALIAS="equalize@1" \
KEY_PASSWORD="your-secure-password" \
node scripts/games/android/run.mjs <slug> --web --gradle
```

Or Gradle directly from the game's `android/` dir:

```bash
export KEYSTORE_PASSWORD="your-secure-password"
export KEY_ALIAS="equalize@1"
export KEY_PASSWORD="your-secure-password"
cd games/<Name>/android
./gradlew :app:bundleRelease
# Output: app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
```

> **Never run `:app:assembleRelease`** for Play Store — upload the `.aab` only.

Before upload: bump `versionCode` (+1) and `versionName` in `app/build.gradle.kts`.

### F. §13 pre-upload audit (required)

On a **clean install** of the **release AAB** (install via `bundletool` or Internal testing track):

| Time | Check |
|------|--------|
| 0:00 | Cold launch, airplane mode — no crash |
| 0:30 | First screen matches screenshot #1 |
| 0:45 | Every home/HUD button cited in listing works |
| 1:00 | One non-obvious listed feature (leaderboard, daily tab, undo) |
| 1:20 | UI matches uploaded screenshots (theme, layout) |
| 2:00 | `adb logcat` — no repeating fatal JS errors |

Fill listing matrix in `docs/play-listings/<slug>.md` (or equivalent). **Do not** claim themes, modes, or leaderboard without discoverable UI (§13).

Re-capture **Play screenshots from release build on emulator** (1080×2400) — preview-server shots are draft only.

### G. Play Console upload (per app)

1. **Create app** → default language → app name matches standalone identity (not portal brand).
2. **Dashboard → Production** (or start with **Internal testing**).
3. **Create new release** → upload `app-release.aab`.
4. Complete required sections (first app takes longest):

| Section | TanStack WebView typical answers |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| **App category** | Game → Puzzle / Casual / etc. |
| **Store listing** | Short + full description from §13 matrix; 512×512 **PNG** icon; feature graphic 1024×500; ≥2 phone screenshots |
| **Content rating** | IARC questionnaire (usually low violence for puzzles) |
| **Target audience** | Age bands per content |
| **Data safety** | No data collected / all on-device if no `INTERNET` and no analytics |
| **Ads** | No (unless added) |
| **Privacy policy** | URL required if any data collected; offline-only games often still need a simple policy page |
| **App access** | All functionality available without login |

5. **Review and roll out** Internal testing first → fix Misleading Claims issues → promote to Production.
6. Update **all active tracks and locales** — stale hi-IN / testing tracks cause rejections (§13).

### H. Post-launch

- Keep `applicationId` stable forever.
- Each update: web build → `versionCode++` → new AAB → release notes cite visible UI changes.
- Do not publish a second app in the same category with duplicate positioning (e.g. Lumen Circuit + Circuit Flow).

